<div id="2026-09-01-queue-reopen-job" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-01 — /3d/queue: reopen a mis-clicked completed/cancelled job</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Added a <em>↩ Reopen</em> action to the Recently Completed table on <code>/3d/queue</code>. Reopening a <code>completed</code> or <code>cancelled</code> job resets it to <code>queued</code> and unwinds the inventory side effects the complete handler applied: the filament <code>issue</code> is reversed with a <code>return</code> transaction and the finished-goods <code>receive</code> is reversed with an <code>issue</code>. Printer depreciation is deliberately NOT reversed (already consumed). The job's cost/time columns and <code>completed_at</code> are cleared, a <code>[ts] Reopened by USER (was STATUS)</code> line is appended to <code>admin_notes</code>, and the printer holding the job goes back to <code>idle</code>.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> Completing the wrong queue row was unrecoverable in the UI — the only actions were assign / complete / cancel, and the completed table carried no download link either. So a mis-clicked completion silently corrupted inventory (phantom finished part + consumed filament) AND dropped the operator's access to the STL. The completed section now also carries the ⬇ Download File / Download 3MF link, and lists <code>cancelled</code> rows alongside <code>completed</code> so a wrongly-cancelled job can be recovered too.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Util/Printing3d.pm</code> (new <code>reopen_job()</code>; 3d.pm is at its size limit), <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/3d.pm</code> (<code>reopen</code> action in the queue POST handler; new <code>return</code> transaction type in <code>_inventory_transaction()</code>; completed-jobs query now selects <code>model_id</code>/<code>source_type</code>/<code>model_file</code> and includes <code>cancelled</code>), <code>root/3d/queue.tt</code> (Action column with download link + Reopen button; heading → "Recently Completed / Cancelled").</p>
</div>
